.TH REMOTERIG-SERVER 1 "September 2026" "RemoteRig 1.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
remoterig\-server \- share an amateur radio transceiver over the network
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B remoterig\-server
.RI [ --list-audio ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Runs next to the transceiver and serves its audio, PTT and CAT control to a
remote client. Radio control goes through Hamlib, or through plain RTS/DTR
toggling on a serial port for rigs without CAT.
.PP
Audio travels over UDP, control over TCP. The PTT is sent on both at once, so a
lost datagram never leaves the rig transmitting.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-list\-audio
Print every audio interface and device PortAudio can see, with the sample rate
each one accepts, then exit. Use this when a device is missing from the lists.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/F4JTV/RemoteRigServer.conf
Settings: radio model, serial port, audio devices, network ports.
.SH NOTES
Opening a serial port requires membership of the
.B dialout
group.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR remoterig-client (1),
.BR rigctl (1)
